; A balance assertion naming a lot still matches the lot when an
; account's `value` sub-directive has given the lot its valuation.
;
; Ledger gives the valuation to the lot itself, which every amount of
; the lot shares, and the lot still answers to the name it was bought
; under: the assertion's 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01], written without the
; valuation, names the lot Assets:Broker holds, which --lots shows as
; {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7})).  3.4.1 checked a balance assertion
; against the account's holdings stripped of their lot annotations
; (#2318, #2355), so an assertion never found the lot it names, valued
; or not; here it stopped with "Balance assertion off by
; 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7})) (expected to see 0)".

account Assets:Broker
    value $7

2020/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Broker    10 AAPL @ $5
    Assets:Cash

2020/01/02 Check
    Assets:Broker    0 AAPL = 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01]

test bal --lots Assets:Broker
10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))  Assets:Broker
end test
